    <width>170</width>
  </widget>
  <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
    <name>v_loeo_detect</name>
    <pv_name>$(P)Stats:LOEODetect</pv_name>
    <x>40</x>
    <y>436</y>
    <width>170</width>
    <height>32</height>
    <font>
      <font family="Source Sans Pro" style="BOLD" size="20.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <foreground_color>
      <color red="150" green="30" blue="30">
      </color>
    </foreground_color>
    <background_color>
      <color red="245" green="225" blue="225">
      </color>
    </background_color>
    <precision>1</precision>
    <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
    <tooltip>Leave-one-event-out recall for leak vs no-leak — the real generalisation number behind the trustworthy LeakDetected output.</tooltip>
  </widget>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>l_loeo_side</name>
    <text>Supply/Return acc (≈chance)</text>
    <x>220</x>
    <y>416</y>
    <width>180</width>
  </widget>
  <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
    <name>v_loeo_side</name>
    <pv_name>$(P)Stats:LOEOSide</pv_name>
    <x>220</x>
    <y>436</y>
    <width>180</width>
    <height>32</height>
    <font>
      <font family="Source Sans Pro" style="BOLD" size="20.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <foreground_color>
      <color red="150" green="30" blue="30">
      </color>
    </foreground_color>
    <background_color>
      <color red="245" green="225" blue="225">
      </color>
    </background_color>
    <precision>1</precision>
    <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
    <tooltip>Supply-vs-Return side accuracy under LOEO. ~50% is near chance — the physical delta (~0.01-0.05 degC) is below PT100 tolerance, so this barely generalises.</tooltip>
  </widget>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>l_loeo_exact</name>
    <text>Exact-location recall</text>
    <x>410</x>
    <y>416</y>
    <width>180</width>
  </widget>
  <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
    <name>v_loeo_exact</name>
